<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moore Town</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Moore Town is the main Windward Maroon community of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-grande">Rio Grande</a> valley of the parish of Portland, below the Blue Mountains. It succeeded Nanny Town, the stronghold of the Maroon leader Nanny, and holds her grave. Its people keep the Kromanti language, songs and drumming, recognised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a> as part of the intangible heritage of humanity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moore-town.jpg" alt="Moore Town" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diego Tirira from Quito, Ecuador · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JM_Moore_Town_1010_(6)_(17070794889).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
